      "editorial": {
        "en": {
          "why_it_matters": "Cityy is interesting because the band starts from instrumental identity rather than a front-person hierarchy: two saxophone voices, keyboards and a bass-led groove have to create the shape of the music together. The quartet is still very young, only active since 2025, and arrives in Yokohama on its first-album cycle; adding Hiroyuki Noritake connects that emerging vocabulary to a deep Japanese fusion lineage without turning the night into a heritage package. This is a chance to hear a new ensemble while its collective language is still becoming visible.",
          "trip_verdict": "Actively make room if you are in Greater Tokyo/Kanto and fusion, saxophone interplay or bass-led groove are part of the listening thread. Yokohama is worth building the evening around, but the Osaka stop four days earlier and the band's active development mean there is no reason to reshape a larger trip around this date alone.",
